WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:05.256
Identify, explain and apply the important ideas behind different types of data.

00:00:06.117 --> 00:00:11.578
Data: raw facts gathered for a purpose. Information: data organised to make sense.

00:00:12.450 --> 00:00:17.670
Survey: asks people selected questions. Observation: records what someone notices.

00:00:17.670 --> 00:00:21.325
Table: arranges facts into rows and columns.

00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:27.213
Collect a few harmless facts about classroom materials, NOT personal details. Make a

00:00:27.213 --> 00:00:32.227
paper chart with the terms Data, Information and Survey; explain what each means.
